--- body ---
## Context
Follow-up to 0306 (#386). The author reviewed the shipped behaviour on 2026-11-09 and ruled that ID
claims are not optional: the PEP (§3, amended in this PR) now says every store has `tickets/.claims/`.
The binary still treats a store without `.claims/` as claims-off: `erg check` passes it silently and
only `erg new` prints a hint. The review also found that the guarantee "a ticket without its claim is
caught" leans on CI (hooks are per clone and do not run on a clean merge), and that
`erg migrate --claims` migrates partway when duplicates remain.

## Author decisions (2026-11-09)
- Claims are required. A store without `.claims/` is noncompliant.
- The `.gitignore` refusal names the fix clearly.
- `erg migrate --claims` prechecks: it lists every blocker and writes nothing until the store is ready.
- Close the CI dependence with local, offline checks (write-verb warnings, a pre-merge-commit hook).
- `erg check` FAILS a store without `.claims/` (not a warning). Confirmed by the author 2026-11-09.
  Why: the vendored binary changes only on a deliberate `erg sync`, so the failure arrives in the
  session that upgraded, with a one-command fix printed; a warning is what let ~50 duplicates reach
  default branches.
- No legacy cruft (author, 2026-11-09): every claims-off code path, test and doc framing goes. No
  "claims on/off" branch survives in the code; a store without `.claims/` is an error, not a mode.
- The repair code is the migration code (author, 2026-11-09): `erg migrate --claims` is the single
  repair path. It prechecks, lists every blocker, writes nothing until ready, and also repairs a
  compliant store with unclaimed tickets (writes the missing claims). Every error message about a
  missing `.claims/` or a missing claim names it; the plain-file `echo` fix may stay alongside so a
  store stays repairable without the binary.

## Design
1. Enforcement. `erg check` fails a store without `.claims/` with one message naming the fix
   (`erg migrate --claims DIR`). `erg new` refuses in such a store with the same message. The
   claims-off post-check retry loop in new.go and its tests are retired: no compliant store reaches it.
   `erg init` on an existing store without `.claims/` says the store must be migrated.
2. Migrate precheck. `erg migrate --claims` first collects every blocker -- each ignored claim path,
   each number shared by two or more tickets (with all their paths) -- prints them all, writes
   nothing, exits 1. Only a clean precheck writes `.claims/` and every claim. Still idempotent.
3. Name the ignore fix. Every refusal over an ignored claim path (new, init, migrate) prints the exact
   lines to add, computed for the store path, e.g. `!tickets/.claims/` and `!tickets/.claims/*`, and
   the file and rule that ignore it (from `git check-ignore -v`).
4. Correct `erg check`'s hint for a duplicated number: renumber all but one clear of the frontier,
   not `echo` a claim (doing that for both tickets of a pair creates a fresh conflict).
5. Write verbs warn. `new`, `close`, `rm`, `archive` print on stderr the tickets of the store that
   have no claim (capped list), so any clone that uses erg sees one, hook or no hook, offline.
6. Merge hook. `erg install --hooks` also installs (or upgrades in place) a managed
   `pre-merge-commit` block running the index check it shares with pre-commit, so a clean merge that
   brings in an unclaimed ticket or two tickets on one number is refused locally. Plain sh and awk,
   no binary; the full corpus check runs at the next ticket commit and in CI. Mirrored byte for byte
   in integration.md.
7. Docs say "required": spec-erg-v1.md, integration.md (drop the "Switching on" framing; collapse the
   catch rules to: `erg new` cannot produce an unclaimed ticket; anything else is reported by the next
   erg command, commit or merge in that clone; CI is a backstop), both AGENTS.md copies (2400-byte
   budget), README, helptext, CHANGELOG (upgrade note: after `erg sync`, run
   `erg migrate --claims`), regenerated manual.
8. Migrate git-erg's own store in this PR (`erg migrate --claims tickets/`), since its check would
   otherwise fail.

## Exit criteria
- [x] `erg check` fails a store without `.claims/`, naming the fix; `erg new` refuses there.
- [x] The claims-off retry loop and its tests are gone; the 10-way race test runs on a claims store.
- [x] `erg migrate --claims` on a store with two duplicate pairs and an ignored path reports all three
      blockers in one run and writes nothing (no `.claims/` created).
- [x] Every ignored-path refusal prints the exact allowlist lines and the ignoring rule.
- [x] `erg check`'s hint for a duplicated number says renumber.
- [x] `new`/`close`/`rm`/`archive` warn about unclaimed tickets; tested.
- [x] `erg install --hooks` installs and upgrades the pre-merge-commit block; a scratch clean merge
      bringing an unclaimed ticket is refused.
- [x] Docs per Design 7 say "required"; no "opt-in"/"switching on" framing left (grep).
- [x] git-erg's own store is migrated; `make check` passes.

## Notes
- Possible monster: 15+ files. If the planner judges so, split hooks/warnings (5, 6) from
  enforcement/migrate/docs (1-4, 7, 8).
- Adopters (the harness, ticket 1472) migrate after syncing a release that carries this.

## Imagine (raid a59e5b, 2026-11-09)
Imagine seat: Claude Opus 5.5. Blind-Spot seat: gpt-6.1-sol (OpenAI, cross-family).

Approach (exit criteria unchanged):
- One `requireClaims(store) error` replaces the `claimsActive` bool; every caller uses it; no mode
  flag survives. Claims-off sites to delete: claims.go:25-29,51,233; new.go:82-89,233-262,271-272;
  nextid.go:269-272; check.go:323; init.go:93-97,589-592,722 (an ignored .claims becomes a refusal);
  install.go:117 and integration.md:66 (`if [ -d tickets/.claims ]`); migrate help "Switch on".
- Verbs in a store without `.claims/`: check fails; new refuses; close/rm/archive warn with the
  migrate command and proceed (refusing would break autoclose right after `erg sync`); list, ready,
  show, validate untouched (they diagnose). Write-verb warnings about unclaimed tickets filter
  `claimViolations`, no new scanner. init on a non-empty store without `.claims/` finishes its asset
  work, prints the migrate command, exits 1; it does not run the precheck. A zero-ticket store fails
  like any; migrate writes only `.keep`. A subdirectory is not a store (help text, no special case).
- Migrate precheck blockers = duplicate IDs + every claim migrate cannot fix (mismatched slug,
  malformed, symlink) + every ignored path. Today `migrateClaims` (claims.go:335-337) counts a
  mismatched EEXIST as "already present": fix. Ignored paths: collect all, not the first
  (`ignoredClaimFile`, claims.go:104); drop `check-ignore -v` lines that match a `!` negation (exit 0);
  report once per rule, allowlist lines relative to the ignoring file named by `-v`.
- Design 4: suppress the claim message for numbers already reported duplicate (validate.go:145); the
  duplicate message carries the renumber hint.
- Fixtures are the real cost: ~18 shell and 8 Go test files build stores without `.claims/`. Add one
  shell helper (plain files, not the binary) and one Go helper; audit every negative test so it fails
  for its intended defect, not for the missing `.claims/` (grep its message, not only the exit code).

Blind-Spot findings folded in:
- Independent migrations conflict: a fresh random nonce per existing ticket makes two clones or
  branches that migrate the same base add/add-conflict on every claim. Make migration claims
  deterministic for tickets that already exist (nonce derived from number, slug and Created, so the
  same ticket gives the same claim everywhere), keep the random nonce for `erg new`; document
  "migrate once on the shared base, then integrate". Test: migrate two branches from one base,
  merge, no conflict.
- The upgrade recipe must install the hooks: `erg sync`, `erg init`, `erg install --hooks`,
  `erg migrate --claims`; migrate's success line names the hook step.
- Merge-time checks must read the committed result, not the working tree: an untracked claim lets
  `erg check` pass while the merge commit lacks it. The pre-merge-commit block (and the pre-commit
  block) check the index: every `tickets/**.erg` in `git ls-files` has its `tickets/.claims/NNNN` in
  the index. Test: merge an unclaimed ticket with a matching untracked claim present; refused.
- Interrupted claim write: the no-hardlink fallback can leave a partial claim; the precheck must name
  a safe recovery (an uncommitted partial claim may be removed, then re-run) rather than dead-end.
- This PR's hooks run the committed old `tickets/erg` (0306) until CI rebuilds it after merge: check
  that the old binary accepts the migrated store and the new assets (run it on the branch tree).

Split: one PR, as the author asked; migrating git-erg's own store is its first implementation commit
(291 generated claims). Later review: 30 days after adopters migrate, count CI-caught claim failures
and write-verb warnings that fired; drop design 5 if none fired.

## Plan (raid a59e5b; Plan seat: Claude Opus 5.5)
Ordered commits, each green, `make docs` in any commit that edits help text (test_docs.sh:46-52):
1. Deterministic migration nonce: `migrationNonce(id, slug, created)` = first 8 hex of
   sha256("NNNN slug Created") (title excluded: branches edit it); `writeClaim` takes the nonce;
   `erg new` keeps the random one; check unchanged (reads first field, needs >= 2 fields). First
   test: literal `migrationNonce("0001","a","2026-11-08")=="b298394c"` (from sha256sum, not the
   function); then test_claims.sh: two branches migrate one plain-file base, merge exits 0, no diff
   under tickets/.claims.
2. Migrate git-erg's own store with the freshly built binary (`build/erg migrate --claims tickets/`),
   not the vendored 0306 one (random nonces). Proof: both `tickets/erg check` and `build/erg check`
   exit 0; a re-run writes 0.
3. Fixture helpers: tests/claims_fixture.sh (sourced, not `test_*`) `claim_store DIR` writes plain
   files (`.keep`, `SLUG 00000000`); Go `claimStore(t, dir)`. Every fixture claimed unless the test
   is about claims. Green on old code; lands before enforcement.
4. `requireClaims` replaces `claimsActive` (claims.go:48-65); message
   `<store> has no .claims/: ID claims are required -- run: erg migrate --claims <store>`; new refuses
   before MkdirAll and loses the retry loop (new.go:233-236,244-264,271-273); init on a populated
   store without .claims/ exits 1 after its asset work; ignored .claims exits 1. First test
   `TestCheckFailsWithoutClaimsDir` (rc 1, message names the command; control after claimStore rc 0);
   new_test.go:279 and test_new.sh:179-250 inverted (10 refusals, 0 files).
5. Migrate precheck: collect blockers (shared numbers, mismatched/malformed/symlinked claims, ignored
   paths), write nothing on any; fix claims.go:342 (mismatched EEXIST counted as present); partial
   untracked claim -> "partial write? rm PATH, re-run"; success line names the hook step. First test:
   pairs 0002, 0004 and `.*` ignored -> rc 1, all four paths and the rule on stderr, no .claims/
   created (exit-code-only would be tautological: old code exits 1 too).
6. `ignoredClaimRules` replaces `ignoredClaimFile` (claims.go:99): `check-ignore -v --stdin`, parse,
   drop `!` patterns, once per source:line, allowlist lines relative to the ignoring file's dir (repo
   top for info/exclude, core.excludesFile). First test: root `.*` -> stderr names `.gitignore:1:.*`
   and the two `!` lines; appending them makes the re-run succeed. Also a nested tickets/.gitignore
   and a negation-only match.
7. Duplicate hint: claimViolations skips numbers held twice; validate.go:145 adds "renumber all but
   one clear of the frontier". Test: one line has "renumber", none has `echo "`.
8. Write-verb warnings: `warnUnclaimed(verb, dir)` filters the unclaimed list (cap 5 + "and N more");
   new/close/rm/archive; without .claims/ they print the migrate command and proceed. Test: hand-made
   0009; `erg close 0001` rc 0, stderr names 0009; claimed control silent.
9. Hooks: one Go constant `claimsIndexCheck` (POSIX sh + awk over `git ls-files -- tickets`,
   `[0-9]` x4 for mawk, `(.*/)?` for closed/) in the pre-commit body and a new pre-merge-commit body
   (which first runs `tickets/erg check tickets/`); `planMergeHook` via `planGitHook`. Fix
   test_selfcoherence.sh:106-133 to compare each block by index and assert two non-empty blocks
   containing `ls-files`. First test: merge an unclaimed ticket with the matching claim untracked on
   disk -> merge refused, MERGE_HEAD present, erg check passes there (proves index). Control: claim
   committed -> merge succeeds. Upgrade keeps third-party content. Doc: fast-forward runs no hook.
10. Docs + CHANGELOG (rewrite the unreleased 0306 entry): spec "required" + derived nonce;
   integration catch rules, "migrate once on the shared base"; both AGENTS.md (2400-byte cap at
   test_integration.sh:108; drop "If `tickets/.claims/` exists,"); README. Ratchet grep:
   `claims are on|switch(es|ing)? (claims )?on|claims off` finds nothing.
Orchestrator amendment: the upgrade recipe is `erg sync`, `erg init`, `erg migrate --claims`, commit,
THEN `erg install --hooks` -- the new pre-commit block rejects every commit in an unmigrated store,
so hooks come after migration; migrate's success line says so.
Old-binary compatibility: `tickets/erg check tickets/` (0306 binary) exits 0 after commits 2, 9, 10,
and `tickets/erg new` works in a scratch clone of the branch.
Done: `make check`; `make test-claims test-new test-check test-init test-install test-hook
test-selfcoherence test-integration test-docs`; `go test ./...`; `tickets/erg check tickets/`.

## Feasibility (raid a59e5b; Sonnet 5.5) -- PASS with WARNs, no BLOCK
- Citations PASS (planGitHook is install.go:268-307; AGENTS.md has 9 bytes of headroom and
  tickets/AGENTS.md must change in lockstep). git-erg's store has no .claims/ yet (290 tickets).
- check-ignore (git 2.43): sources are repo-top-relative (`tickets/.gitignore:1:...`), but
  `.git/info/exclude` is absolute in a linked worktree and core.excludesFile is always absolute:
  the step-6 parser handles both. Negation matches print with `!`, rc 0: dropping them is needed.
- awk: mawk, busybox and nawk agree on a sample (closed/, 5-digit name, .keep). Embed the literal
  program in the plan/test. `[0-9]` x4 stays.
- Hooks: clean `merge --no-ff` runs pre-merge-commit; failure leaves MERGE_HEAD; fast-forward and
  --no-verify skip it; concluding a refused merge with `git commit` runs pre-commit only, so the
  pre-commit index check is the backstop.
- Nonce literal verified; hash without a trailing newline (with one it is c17056d6).
- Missed sites: `ensureClaimsDir` (claims.go:202) and migrate.go:666 also call the replaced
  functions; tests creating tickets with erg new/cmdNew need claim fixtures too: test_pipeline,
  test_strictwrite, test_roundtrip, test_stderr, test_security, claims_test, resolve_test; install
  help (21-28) and summary strings, integration.md uninstall (304-315), test_install.sh 278-353 gain
  pre-merge-commit; `make docs` regenerates the manual and spec copies.
